{
 "source": "frames_cosmetic_a.png",
 "notes": [
  "S4a: the six portrait frames the cosmetics catalogue names (balance/cosmetics.json `art`: frames/<id>), each painted twice -- a square frame (left) and a ring (right) -- on the flat navy ground, keyed off it (darkkey against the sheet's own ground, [9,19,29]); the EMPTY windows key clear with the ground, so a portrait drawn under a frame shows through.",
  "frames/<id>_square and frames/<id>_ring are the brief's sizes, 'paint big, draw down': one scale per kind, so every plain band comes out the same size -- a square's band 160 outer (253 painted), a ring's 96 (232 painted) -- and a frame's ornaments (the patron's crown, the aureole's rays) stand outside it. Each crop is centred on the frame's own window, so the asset's centre is the portrait's centre on every frame; its neighbours' ink is masked off (the aureole's rays reach up into the patron's cell).",
  "frames/<id>_tile is the ring whole, fitted into the wardrobe tile's 224x190 art box (above its name plate), as wardrobe.png draws them: every frame at one outer size, ornaments included.",
  "Measured with scratchpad scans of the sheet: ink bboxes against the ground (distance > 40) and each window's centre from its inner edges along the centre lines."
 ],
